                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9abec06-c39b-3eac-a9d6-bc708e76ddd3",
                        "entry_id": "9a41e2ca-b540-348c-a786-16b074db30f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to shame, to disgrace, to dishonor"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de28550a-bab9-4778-a5b1-e1e8203f4f7d",
                                "sense_id": "e9abec06-c39b-3eac-a9d6-bc708e76ddd3",
                                "text": "«Да, он о́чень краси́в, ду́мал Пьер, я зна́ю его́. Для него́ была́ бы осо́бенная пре́лесть в том, чтоб осрами́ть моё и́мя и посмея́ться надо мной, и́менно потому́, что я хлопота́л за него́ и призре́л его́, помо́г ему́.",
                                "translation": "“Yes, he is very handsome,” thought Pierre, “and I know him. It would be particularly pleasant to him to dishonor my name and ridicule me, just because I have exerted myself on his behalf, befriended him, and helped him.",
                                "english": "“Yes, he is very handsome,” thought Pierre, “and I know him. It would be particularly pleasant to him to dishonor my name and ridicule me, just because I have exerted myself on his behalf, befriended him, and helped him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
